<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Named functions map onto the Jacobian, the growth-rate peak, the IMEX step, the chronoseries, the ablation, and the plate comparison. Loop_3220 proves the determinant, the trace, the Dv/Du = 20 drive, the equal-diffusion failure, the wavelength order, and the eight-mode count, with no sorry. The integer Jacobian is the script's floating-point Jacobian scaled by 10." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Jacobian, sigma_+, the diffusivity solve, and the spectral IMEX step implement Schnakenberg kinetics and Turing's dispersion relation. k_c is argmax sigma_+, distinct from Murray's k_m (wavelength 130.6 µm versus 164.37 µm). The equal-diffusion control returns max sigma = -0.105, which is the sign Turing's necessary condition requires. Ten points are withheld because the 164.3 µm target is the slot's assigned scale, not a wavelength estimated from a measured coat, and because the time step is first-order IMEX." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion Pearson r = 0.993406 against a reference of 1, RMSE = 0.037048 against 0. Nonlinear stripe wavelength 167.9414 µm against the assigned 164.3 µm. Ablation max growth -0.105 against 0. Pliohippus and quagga linear peaks differ from their targets in the fourth significant figure. Horsfall coherency 0.5235 against the simulation coherency 0.8209. Radial KS 0.9575 against 0. None of these values is a copy of its reference. The KS is a real disagreement, not a fitted success, so the dimension does not get a score in the mid-90s." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
