        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the pass-1 Schnakenberg solve (linear peak 164.37 µm, nonlinear wavelength 167.94 µm, dispersion Pearson r = 0.993, RMSE = 0.037) and adds the three chronospecies targets (Pliohippus 198.70 µm, Scotti 164.31 µm, Quagga 400.01 µm), a Dv/Du sweep at fixed Du on which lambda rises from 134.6 µm to 190.1 µm, an equal-diffusion ablation whose maximum growth rate is -0.105, and a radial-spectrum KS distance of 0.957 between the Horsfall plate and the activator. The KS is large on purpose: the plate is a whole-animal drawing and the field is a spot lattice. Overall 86.4/100 (faithfulness 85.6, reproducibility 88.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 3d4615e96e7fbafcf9d3e24355fcc03695e61f40; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/equus_scotti_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 3d4615e96e7fbafcf9d3e24355fcc03695e61f40, image/png, 392198 B, 1584×946 px, artifact_sha256 003c2e77dd423d8d470005fc1556382940fa073d32ddae515bf7997517b03f56 (sha256 003c2e77dd423d8d470005fc1556382940fa073d32ddae515bf7997517b03f56), spec_fingerprint a3ff127a4fbe604c383fca881bbb59ca1298842374b9b9112403cb1ca2e31003. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a3ff127a4fbe604c383fca881bbb59ca1298842374b9b9112403cb1ca2e31003; artifact_sha256: 003c2e77dd423d8d470005fc1556382940fa073d32ddae515bf7997517b03f56. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability; equal diffusivities do not select a finite wavelength. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-substrate kinetics with the u^2 v term. | Bard 1977: equid initiation spacing about 0.4 mm; week 3 for the plains zebra. | Bard 1981: pale bands are melanin inhibition on a dark ground. | Murray 1981: domain size relative to wavelength sets the mode count. | MacFadden 1986: equid body size increases from Hyracotherium to Equus.; reconstructed_in_script: Du, Dv at Dv/Du = 20 solved so argmax sigma_+ is 164.3 µm. | Pliohippus wavelength 198.7 µm = 164.3 µm times the catalog length ratio 0.260/0.215. | Quagga wavelength set to Bard's 400 µm by solving a separate Du at Dv/Du = 30. | Flank overlay and the KS comparison against the Horsfall plate.; transfer_boundary: 164.3 µm is the assigned scale of this slot. It was not measured on a fossil coat. | The campaign chronoseries places Equus quagga after Equus scotti. That is not a cladogram.; does_not_claim: That 164 µm was measured on Equus scotti. | That the Horsfall pencil texture is a melanocyte lattice. The KS distance 0.957 records the mismatch. | That Pliohippus coat spacing was observed.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.64e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "At the scotti diffusivity, raising Dv/Du from 8 to 40 lengthens the linear wavelength monotonically from 134.6 µm to 190.1 µm. The three named targets are hit by solving Du: Pliohippus 198.70 µm (target 198.69), Scotti 164.31 µm (target 164.3), Quagga 400.01 µm (target 400). The order is quagga longer than pliohippus longer than scotti." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
