<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The specimen is Horsfall's 1905 public-domain restoration. The comparison figure shows the plate, the activator lattice, and a feathered flank overlay, and the 12-frame 960×649 GIF grows that overlay. Computer-vision similarity of the GIF's last frame against the plate is 96 because the horse is preserved. The radial-spectrum KS between the raw activator and the plate is 0.957: the spot lattice does not reproduce the drawing's pencil spectrum, and the audit does not treat that KS as a close match. Twenty points are withheld for that scale gap (a whole-animal plate versus a 164 µm field)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) (Equus scotti)",
        "Equus scotti follicular Turing wavelength at 164 µm (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma) faithfully reproduces Equus scotti morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Equus scotti specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Equus scotti" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 164 µm was measured on Equus scotti.",
        "does_not_claim: That Pliohippus coat spacing was observed.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Horsfall pencil texture is a melanocyte lattice. The KS distance 0.957 records the mismatch.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du, Dv at Dv/Du = 20 solved so argmax sigma_+ is 164.3 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Flank overlay and the KS comparison against the Horsfall plate.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pliohippus wavelength 198.7 µm = 164.3 µm times the catalog length ratio 0.260/0.215.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Quagga wavelength set to Bard's 400 µm by solving a separate Du at Dv/Du = 30.",
        "reported_in_source: Bard 1977: equid initiation spacing about 0.4 mm; week 3 for the plains zebra.",
        "reported_in_source: Bard 1981: pale bands are melanin inhibition on a dark ground.",
        "reported_in_source: MacFadden 1986: equid body size increases from Hyracotherium to Equus.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: domain size relative to wavelength sets the mode count.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: activator-substrate kinetics with the u^2 v term.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability; equal diffusivities do not select a finite wavelength.",
        "transfer_boundary: 164.3 µm is the assigned scale of this slot. It was not measured on a fossil coat.",
        "transfer_boundary: The campaign chronoseries places Equus quagga after Equus scotti. That is not a cladogram." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Equus scotti (Middle Pleistocene (Irvingtonian, 0.6 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Equus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-equus-scotti-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/equus_scotti_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Equus scotti; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability; equal diffusivities do not select a finite wavelength. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-substrate kinetics with the u^2 v term. | Bard 1977: equid initiation spacing about 0.4 mm; week 3 for the plains zebra. | Bard 1981: pale bands are melanin inhibition on a dark ground. | Murray 1981: domain size relative to wavelength sets the mode count. | MacFadden 1986: equid body size increases from Hyracotherium to Equus.; reconstructed_in_script: Du, Dv at Dv/Du = 20 solved so argmax sigma_+ is 164.3 µm. | Pliohippus wavelength 198.7 µm = 164.3 µm times the catalog length ratio 0.260/0.215. | Quagga wavelength set to Bard's 400 µm by solving a separate Du at Dv/Du = 30. | Flank overlay and the KS comparison against the Horsfall plate.; transfer_boundary: 164.3 µm is the assigned scale of this slot. It was not measured on a fossil coat. | The campaign chronoseries places Equus quagga after Equus scotti. That is not a cladogram.; does_not_claim: That 164 µm was measured on Equus scotti. | That the Horsfall pencil texture is a melanocyte lattice. The KS distance 0.957 records the mismatch. | That Pliohippus coat spacing was observed.]; phenomenon_size: 2.1 mm (0.00213 m, log10=-2.672 m, tier=6_organ_mm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 2.1 mm to 3.41 m): 2.1 mm:equus-quagga-bioelectric-polarity, 4.0 mm:equus-quagga-vertex-packing, 7.6 cm:equus-quagga-turing-wavelength, 13.9 cm:equus-quagga-clock-wavefront, 45.1 cm:equus-quagga-morphogen-condensation, 58.9 cm:equus-quagga-flux-canalization, 62.0 cm:equus-quagga-elastic-buckling, 77.0 cm:equus-quagga-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90109-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
